  "Question": "Let \\(x_1\\) and \\(x_2\\) be such that \\(x_1\\ne x_2\\) and \\(3x_i^2-hx_i=b,\\) \\(i=1,\\) \\(2.\\) Then \\(x_1+x_2\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-\\frac h3\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac h3\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac b3\\)",
    "D": "\\(2b\\)",
    "E": "\\(-\\frac b3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Both given expressions equal \\(b\\), so subtracting them removes \\(b\\):\n\\[\n3(x_1^2-x_2^2)-h(x_1-x_2)=0.\n\\]\nThe difference-of-squares identity reveals the common factor \\(x_1-x_2\\):\n\\[\n(x_1-x_2)\\bigl[3(x_1+x_2)-h\\bigr]=0.\n\\]\nBecause \\(x_1\\ne x_2\\), we may divide by \\(x_1-x_2\\). Thus \\(3(x_1+x_2)=h\\), giving\n\\[\n\\boxed{x_1+x_2=\\frac h3},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
